<newsitem itemid="191912" id="root" date="1996-11-15" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: General Cable loss deepens, customers up.</title>
<headline>General Cable loss deepens, customers up.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence) loss	 7.4		    vs 6.2 loss</p>
<p> Pretax loss		21.17		  vs 16.04 loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   36.57		  vs 22.42</p>
<p>NOTE - General Cable Plc said it has 157,000 residential telephone lines, up 40 percent, and 135,000 cable TV subscribers, up 35 percent.  </p>
<p> Operating loss	   19.13		  vs 14.85 loss</p>
<p> Costs			22.22		  vs 12.98</p>
<p> Tax credit		 0.22		   vs 2.31</p>
<p> Net taxed loss	   21.89		  vs 14.25 loss</p>
<p> Retained loss	    20.28		  vs 13.42 loss</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 77717.</p>
</text>
